---
import DocsLayout from "@/layouts/DocsLayout.astro"

const html =
  '<p>KoAkademy ships six source-tree modules that extend the platform for institutions that need them. Standalone Composer modules can add further domains without copying source into the core repository. Modules are enabled or disabled per installation by your system administrator; some areas additionally depend on feature toggles in General Settings. If your school does not use a module, its pages and menus are hidden entirely.</p>\n<h2>Announcements</h2>\n<p>School-wide announcements targeted at staff, faculty, or students.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Administrators create, schedule, and publish announcements from the administration panel.</li>\n<li>Active announcements appear as a <strong>banner</strong> in the administration panel and on the <strong>student portal</strong> dashboard and announcements page.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Forms</h2>\n<p>The standalone Forms module supports configurable surveys, evaluations, student\ninformation updates, and other school workflows.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Forms can require an authenticated account, identify a guest by e-mail or\nstudent ID, or accept anonymous responses.</li>\n<li>Administrators can define text, choice, date, rating, upload, and other field\ntypes, response policies, close dates, and review workflows.</li>\n<li>Responses can remain linked to the submitting user and can be mapped to\napproved KoAkademy student fields before an administrator applies changes.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Forms must be installed in the application image with Composer before it can be\nenabled. See <a href="/docs/maintainers/module-registry">Module Registry</a> for the\ninstallation and deployment sequence.</p>\n<h2>Cashier</h2>\n<p>A dedicated workspace for cashier staff, separate from the full finance administration area.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Student lookup</strong> with Current Balance, History, and Transactions tabs.</li>\n<li><strong>Payment posting</strong> against outstanding assessments.</li>\n<li>Works together with statements of account and the enrollment payment-verification step.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Inventory</h2>\n<p>Property and equipment management for the school.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Catalog of <strong>products</strong>, <strong>categories</strong>, and <strong>suppliers</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Stock movements</strong> and amendments with a full inventory ledger.</li>\n<li><strong>Borrowings</strong> — track equipment lent to staff or students and its return status.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Library System</h2>\n<p>Library operations for school librarians.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Books</strong>, <strong>authors</strong>, and <strong>categories</strong> catalog management.</li>\n<li><strong>Borrow records</strong> — check books in and out and track overdue items.</li>\n<li><strong>Research papers</strong> repository for the institution&#39;s archive.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Notification Center</h2>\n<p>Template-based messaging to keep the school community informed.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Prebuilt <strong>templates</strong> for common situations: enrollment updates, grade releases, payment notices, class suspensions, holidays, school events, reminders, warnings, and official announcements.</li>\n<li><strong>Bulk sending</strong> to selected audiences, processed in the background.</li>\n<li>Delivered to the recipient&#39;s portal Notification Center and by e-mail where configured.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Student Medical Records</h2>\n<p>Clinic visit records managed by authorized medical staff.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Visit records with type, status, and priority, plus <strong>follow-up scheduling</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Confidentiality flags</strong> restrict sensitive records to authorized personnel.</li>\n<li>A dashboard widget summarizes clinic activity.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class="doc-callout doc-callout-caution">\n  <p class="doc-callout-label">Privacy</p><p>Medical records contain sensitive personal data. Access is limited by role and confidentiality flags — do not grant the medical records permissions to general administrative accounts.</p>\n</div><h2>Enabling or disabling a module</h2>\n<p>Open <strong>Administrators → Marketplace</strong> to enable or disable an installed module.\nThe Marketplace also reports the signed registry catalog and compatibility\nstatus, but it does not install Composer packages or update a running\ncontainer. A standalone module must be added to the application, included in a\nnew image, and migrated before it can be enabled.</p>\n<p>Existing module status choices are preserved during upgrades. The six bundled\nmodules ship enabled for backward-compatible installations; a newly installed\nstandalone module may appear disabled until a super administrator enables it.\nSome areas additionally depend on feature toggles in <strong>General Settings</strong> —\nfor example the inventory and library modules, the student portal, online\nenrollment, clearances, signature capture, and QR codes.</p>\n'
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Optional Modules"
  path="/docs/user-guide/modules"
  description="Bundled and standalone KoAkademy modules, including Announcements, Forms, Cashier, Inventory, Library, Notification Center, and Student Medical Records."
>
  <Fragment set:html={html} />
</DocsLayout>
